    {
      "id": 486234,
      "username": "saaad_asiiif",
      "name": "Saad Asif",
      "created_at": "2025-11-12T07:07:35.592Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hii there !</p>\n<p>The messages you’re seeing are very common for new implementations, so nothing to worry this is just a standard part of the setup process. These are not system errors but <strong>permission issues</strong>.</p>\n<p>Essentially, your user account <strong>it@esai.sv</strong> in your example pictures does not have the necessary roles assigned to it to view specific documents (like Opportunity, Bin, Sales Order, etc.).</p>\n<p>In ERPNext, access to documents and reports is controlled by <strong>Roles</strong> and <strong>Role Permissions Manager</strong>. Your user needs the correct roles, and those roles need to have permissions defined for the specific documents.</p>\n<p>A quick way to get started is to assign the <strong>System Manager</strong> role to your primary admin user. This role typically has access to everything. However, for production, it’s best practice to assign only the necessary roles for security.</p>",
